/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ IPC server half. Requires the `ipc` feature (off by default).
/
/ This script alone just sets up the demo tables — the actual `\port` command
/ has to be typed at the REPL prompt (or piped after this script runs), since
/ opening a port only makes sense in a long-lived interactive session. Run:
/
/   cargo run --features ipc -- -i --load-demo examples/ipc_server.qpl
/   qpl) \port 5001
/
/ Then, in another terminal, run examples/ipc_client.qpl against it.
/ `\port` (no argument) closes the listener again.
/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

log "demo tables `trades` / `quotes` are ready — now run: \\port 5001"
